Subject: [PATCH] fritchii-probeclamp: the storage binding's mapping size is clamped to 32 bits before it is

fritchii-probeclamp: the storage binding's mapping size is clamped to 32 bits before it is
narrowed, and a doubling-count log line says when that happens.
Switch EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PROBECLAMP=1, off by default (Common::PeSwitch).

Upstream: Frizti/Fritchii 8193f926fa "buffer_cache: bind table-pointer pools as far as a storage
buffer reaches" (jpkto, zortos293/Lichii#351, cherry-pick of b72195422b, fritchii-v4): "The mapping
size is clamped to 32 bits before it is narrowed."

What: StorageBufferBinding narrowed MemoryManager::GetMemoryLayoutSize (a size_t, the run of
same-kind mapping from the pointer: kind_map.GetContinuousSizeFrom) straight to u32
(buffer_cache.h:3837). A run of 4 GiB or more kept only its size modulo 4 GiB, so a read-only
table pointer could be bound to a few bytes instead of EDEN_NX2_TABLE_POOL_MIB, and the packed-size
test compared against the wrapped value. With the switch the size is min(size, 0xFFFFFFFF) first;
every later cap (TABLE_POOL_MIB, the 8 MiB native/default caps, packed_size <= size) applies as
before. When the clamp changes a value it logs "Storage binding mapping clamped to 4 GiB: N so far"
(count 1, 2, 4, 8, ...) with the mapping size and the old narrowed size, so one PS5 run shows
whether Ocarina has such mappings at all.

Gated rather than unconditional on purpose: on the PS5 a wrapped (small) binding may currently be
what keeps a pool binding small; un-wrapping it can grow that binding to the TABLE_POOL_MIB cap
(128 MiB in the play env), which matters at 266 MiB free. Unset: narrowed as before, no log.

Not ported (and not needed): the rest of #351, binding read-only table pointers to
min(maxStorageBufferRange, 1 GiB) - 64 KiB. That is our 0201 EDEN_NX2_TABLE_POOL_MIB (0..1024
MiB). Fritchii measured Hyrule Field light probes up to about 130 MiB past the pool pointer, so the
play env's 128 can still miss the farthest cells (white haze / exposure jumps at the field's
edges): test EDEN_NX2_TABLE_POOL_MIB=160 with a Hyrule Field picture check. The OpenGL halves of
#351 are not used on the PS5.

diff --git a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
index c709c1b..48004b9 100644
--- a/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/buffer_cache/buffer_cache.h
@@ -3833,8 +3833,25 @@ Binding BufferCache<P>::StorageBufferBinding(GPUVAddr ssbo_addr, u32 cbuf_index,
     }
     const Binding binding = [&]() -> Binding {
         u32 size = [&]() {
+            const u64 layout_size = static_cast<u64>(gpu_memory->GetMemoryLayoutSize(gpu_addr));
+            // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PROBECLAMP=1 (Fritchii 8193f926fa, zortos293/Lichii#351): the
+            // mapping size is clamped to 32 bits before it is narrowed. Unset: narrowed directly,
+            // as before, so a mapping of 4 GiB or more keeps only its size modulo 4 GiB.
+            static const bool clamp_layout = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_PROBECLAMP");
             const u32 memory_layout_size =
-                static_cast<u32>(gpu_memory->GetMemoryLayoutSize(gpu_addr));
+                clamp_layout ? static_cast<u32>((std::min)(layout_size, u64{0xFFFF'FFFFULL}))
+                             : static_cast<u32>(layout_size);
+            if (clamp_layout && layout_size > u64{0xFFFF'FFFFULL}) {
+                // The log thins out as the count doubles.
+                static std::atomic<u64> clamped_layouts{};
+                const u64 count = clamped_layouts.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed) + 1;
+                if ((count & (count - 1)) == 0) {
+                    LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                             "Storage binding mapping clamped to 4 GiB: {} so far; last {} MiB "
+                             "at {:#x}, narrowed it was {} bytes",
+                             count, layout_size >> 20, gpu_addr, static_cast<u32>(layout_size));
+                }
+            }
             // A pointer read from a table in memory is the base of an object pool, read anywhere
             // in it (Ocarina of Time's grass instances lie 12-18 MiB past theirs). With
             // EDEN_NX2_TABLE_POOL_MIB=64 a read-only one is bound to the end of its mapping, up
